-- title:
--   §4.2.1, proof of Theorem 3.3, (4.5) — if ‖x*‖₀ < s then f(x*) ≤ f(x* + teᵢ) for every i ∈ I₀(x*) and t
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ be continuously differentiable and bounded below (Assumption 1), let $0<s<n$ be an integer, and let $(x^k)$ be a sequence generated by the greedy sparse-simplex method for (P). Let $x^*$ be an accumulation point of $(x^k)$ with $\|x^*\|_0<s$, and let $i\in I_0(x^*)$, i.e. $x^*_i=0$. Then
--   $$f(x^*)\le f(x^*+te_i)\qquad\text{for all } t\in\mathbb R .$$
--
--   This is the off-support half of the case $\|x^*\|_0<s$ in the proof of Theorem 3.3. Together with (4.2) it gives Case I of the definition of a CW-minimum. The difficulty is that iterates near $x^*$ may sit at the sparsity level $s$, where the method cannot simply add the coordinate $e_i$ and must instead swap out a support coordinate whose value tends to zero.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Accumulation point" is `MapClusterPt xstar atTop x`. Indices are $0,\dots,n-1$ and $te_i$ is `EuclideanSpace.single i t`. Assumption 1 is the paper's standing assumption.
-- source:
--   Beck, Eldar, Sparsity Constrained Nonlinear Optimization: Optimality Conditions and Algorithms, SIAM J. Optim. (2013), doi:10.1137/120869778 (source: arXiv:1203.4580v1), p. 30, §4.2.1, proof of Theorem 3.3, (4.3)–(4.5) and the display after (4.5)

import Definitions.Def_SparseNLO_Greedy_Method

open Filter Topology

namespace SparseNLO.Greedy

/-- §4.2.1, proof of Theorem 3.3, (4.5) and the display after it (p. 30): if `x*` is an
accumulation point of a run of the greedy sparse-simplex method with `‖x*‖₀ < s`, then for every
`i ∈ I₀(x*)`, `f(x*) ≤ f(x* + t eᵢ)` for all `t ∈ ℝ`. -/
theorem eq_4_5
    {n s : ℕ} (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f)
    (hbdd : ∃ γ : ℝ, ∀ x, γ ≤ f x) (hs : 0 < s) (hsn : s < n)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hrun : IsGreedyRun f s x)
    (xstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hacc : MapClusterPt xstar atTop x)
    (hstar : SparseNLO.CWOpt.l0 xstar < s) (i : Fin n) (hi : i ∈ SparseNLO.CWOpt.I0 xstar) :
    ∀ t : ℝ, f xstar ≤ f (xstar + EuclideanSpace.single i t) := by sorry

end SparseNLO.Greedy
